Components in React JS

A Component is a reusable piece of UI (User Interface). React applications are built by combining multiple components.
OR
"A React Component is an independent and reusable piece of UI that returns JSX and can be used multiple times within an application."

Think of components like LEGO blocks:
Navbar → Component
Login Form → Component
Button → Component
Footer → Component

Types of Components
1. Functional Components
2. Class Components

Component with Props
Props are used to pass data from parent to child component.

Important Points

 Props are read-only (cannot be modified by the child).

 Used to send data Parent → Child.

Props can be:
String,Number,Boolean,Array,Object,Function